**Issue Title:** Thrive Funded Retail Price Instead of Invoice Price — Financial Discrepancy
**Category:** Integration Issues
**Description:** For certain apps, Thrive funded the full retail price rather than the actual invoice/job cost. This created overpayments that required contractors to send money back via bank transfer, with Thrive then adjusting the contract amount.
**Supporting Context:** Vipin Mamidi (2/2): "This is one of those apps for which thrive funded the retail price instead of the actual invoices. Sriram is checking with Thrive on what we can do about these apps." Jason Duval outlined the complex resolution process: contractor sends funds back to Thrive, Thrive adjusts contract and refunds any overpayments.
**Potential Product Impact:** Significant financial process failure; requires multi-party coordination (contractor, Thrive, customer) to resolve; indicates data mapping issue between portal retail price and invoice price.

---

**Issue Title:** Momnt API Integration Failure — Charge Request Flow Broken
**Category:** Integration Issues
**Description:** Momnt's API was returning failures, blocking charge requests from being initiated or processed. Separately, Momnt's mandatory welcome call requirement was not visible in the portal, causing unexplained "unable to transact" errors.
**Supporting Context:** Multiple instances (2/3, 2/9). "Yes, it was caught up on the lender's side and I was able to push it through." Sphoorthi: "We recently got to know that Momnt does something called a mandatory welcome call with the customer and if its not done yet, they will temporarily disable the ability to transact."
**Potential Product Impact:** Charge requests fail silently; portal does not surface Momnt's pre-conditions (welcome call completion) to reps or customers; support overhead is high.

